Z||000000||sqoach||03-01-2001||07:14 PM||||what's up? ok, i'm about to by an amp kit from crutchfield, and i know you just got one. is it a pretty good kit? just need some input before i buy one.<P>also, it doesn't look like it has a water-proof fuse holder. how do you have yours to where it won't get rained on?<BR>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 03-01-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Standard||03-01-2001||10:48 PM||||Yep, I got the Scosche EFX 10 gauge wiring kit.  The only problems I had with it was the ring terminals for the power cable was too wide to fit into the power terminal on my amp, and I had to ream it out a little to attach it to the battery.  It might be worth getting the sidemount terminal adaptor, but it's worked fine for my without it.  You'll get enough power and ground cable to do at least 2 cars.<P>I never thought about the water-proof fuse thing... I just zip tied it onto a cable in front of the battery next to those wiring harness connectors.  I looped some cable there so I could re-route it if I had to.  Actually, the fuse holder looks water-proof enough, the cap fits over the fuse pretty tight and it looks like it's sealed to the wire from the factory.   <p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 03-01-2001).]||||reg||1
